From: Zakk <zakk@gentoozh.org>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: wcss-sec: update to v14

The generic kernel patches carry an older revision of the secure WCSS
PIL driver (830-03, 830-04). IPQ5332 runs v14 of the upstream
submission (Vignesh Viswanathan, 2026-08-03), which the 2010a-2010c
patches build on. Update the driver to v14 and keep the split firmware
support of 830-04, so IPQ9574 still loads its auxiliary firmware.

v14 drops the TME-L path, used only by IPQ5424, and changes:
- start: shut the PAS down on a start timeout and keep the q6 prepared
  after a successful start
- stop: request a graceful stop before the PAS shutdown
- da_to_va and coredump: treat the carveout as I/O memory
- map the carveout through of_reserved_mem_region_to_resource()
- take auto_boot from the match data and unwind the subdevices when
  rproc_add fails

Signed-off-by: Zakk <zakk@gentoozh.org>
---
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/Kconfig
@@ -260,6 +260,7 @@ config QCOM_Q6V5_WCSS_SEC
 	depends on QCOM_SMEM
 	depends on RPMSG_QCOM_GLINK_SMEM || RPMSG_QCOM_GLINK_SMEM=n
 	depends on RPMSG_QCOM_GLINK || RPMSG_QCOM_GLINK=n
+	depends on QCOM_AOSS_QMP || QCOM_AOSS_QMP=n
 	select QCOM_MDT_LOADER
 	select QCOM_PIL_INFO
 	select QCOM_Q6V5_COMMON
